.TH KANBAN 1 "August 2026" "kanban" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
kanban \- launch the local Kanban board
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kanban
.RI [ --port " " number|auto ]
.RI [ --no-open ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B kanban
starts the local Kanban runtime server and serves the web UI. It is the board
launcher only; agent task and log operations are provided by the
.B kanban-mcp
stdio server.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --port <number|auto>
Bind to a specific local port or select the first available port starting at 3484.
.TP
.B --no-open
Do not open the browser automatically.
.TP
.B --help, -h
Show help text and exit.
.TP
.B --version, -v
Show version and exit.
.SH MCP
Register the agent-facing server with Codex after installing Kanban:
.PP
.B codex mcp add kanban -- kanban-mcp
.PP
The MCP exposes Kanban task lifecycle, urgent notification, and bounded log
snapshot tools. See
.I docs/mcp.md
in the Kanban distribution for the full tool reference. Destructive task trash
and delete actions require explicit user confirmation.
.SH INTERNAL HOOKS
.B kanban-hooks
is reserved for Kanban's internal agent hook transport. It is not an agent task API.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Start the board:
.B kanban
.TP
Start without opening a browser:
.B kanban --no-open
.TP
Start on a custom port:
.B kanban --port 9000
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR npm (1)
